# Typical Workflow

```
Administrator Creates User
          │
          ▼
Assign Role
          │
          ▼
Configure Permissions
          │
          ▼
Assign Territory / Batch
          │
          ▼
User Reviews Applicants
          │
          ▼
Actions Recorded Across System
```

---

# Common Use Cases

- Control access to application features.
- Assign applicants and processing queues.
- Manage reviewer responsibilities.
- Record which user performed workflow actions.
- Restrict exports and sensitive data access.
- Support operational auditing and accountability.

---

# Why This Table Exists

Rather than embedding user names throughout the application, the system centralizes user information, roles, and permissions in a dedicated table. This enables consistent access control, easier administration, and reliable auditing of user actions across the platform.